      "message": "If we remove this then we have another bug -- multi-byte memmap variables may be updated in between ACPI byte reads. How about this instead?\n\n- If the mutex is unlocked, we lock it from interrupt context.\n- Otherwise, we disable the acpi_0_interrupt, and kick off a new deferred task.\n- The deferred task locks the mutex and re-enables acpi_0_interrupt.\n- We can still unlock the mutex from interrupt context.\n\nWhat do you think?",
